Publishing the Scoop bucket
===========================

luvie.json here is the master copy. The published copy lives in a separate
repository, because that is what Scoop consumes:

    https://github.com/benbriedis/scoop-luvie      bucket/luvie.json

Users then install with

    scoop bucket add luvie https://github.com/benbriedis/scoop-luvie
    scoop install luvie

which is worth having for one reason beyond convenience: Scoop does not set
mark-of-the-web on what it downloads, so this is the only way to install Luvie
on Windows with no SmartScreen warning at all while the binaries are unsigned.
It also puts luvie.lv2 into %APPDATA%\LV2 and takes it away again on uninstall.


Why a bucket of our own
-----------------------

The alternative is submitting to Scoop's `extras` bucket, and winget's
community repository is the same trade. Both mean a moderated pull request per
release. A bucket we own has none of that, and the manifest below updates
itself.


Per release: nothing
--------------------

The manifest carries `checkver` and `autoupdate`, so Scoop derives the new
version, URL, hash and extract_dir from the GitHub releases feed on its own.
There is no per-release step. If you want to update the bucket by hand rather
than wait:

    git clone https://github.com/benbriedis/scoop-luvie
    cd scoop-luvie
    scoop checkver bucket/luvie.json . -u
    git commit -am "luvie: update to 0.0.5" && git push

That command is also how to fill in the placeholder hash in this master copy if
the two ever need to be reconciled.


Keep in step
------------

The URL and extract_dir templates encode the release archive's filename, which
comes from CPACK_PACKAGE_FILE_NAME in cmake/Packaging.cmake:

    luvie-<git describe>-windows-x86_64.zip

Note the "v": the version in the filename is the raw tag, while Scoop's
$version has the prefix stripped, hence "luvie-v$version-..." in the templates.
The archive also has a top-level directory of the same name, which is what
extract_dir strips. Anything that changes that naming, or the bin/ and
lib/lv2/ layout inside the archive, has to be reflected here.
